          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p
            There is a battery of little
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set-theoretic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lemmas"} lemmas
            which inevitably recur when laying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            of core
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
            operators, especially regarding their preservation (or not) of set-theoretic operations like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
          %p
            The attitude and approach of the mathematics professor toward such routine bread-and-butter issues is a matter of some interest. A professional, upon being presented with any one of these “naive set theory”
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            = succeed "," do
              %em explanation
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          %p
            A strong pedagogy would not only instill this sort of basic training, but make the battery of routine results more memorable by concentrating their essence in one or two basic principles that provide an explanatory basis for the rest. According to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lawvere69"} Lawvere 69
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lawvere05"} Lawvere 05
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjoint
            relationships front and center and seeing how the rest flows from them is an effective way to arrange the facts.
