              is the fact that
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} left adjoints preserve colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              preserves unions and intersections is that in addition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints+preserve+limits"} right adjoints preserve limits
          %h2#projection_formula Projection formula
          %p
            Another useful formula for interactions between images and pre-images and intersections is the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+formula"} projection formula
          %p
          #ProjectionFormulaForFunctionsAndInverseImages.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \,\colon\, X \to Y
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subseteq X,\; T \subseteq Y
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f\big(
                    S \cap f^{-1}(T)
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    f(S) \cap T
                    \\,.
            %p
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Lee00"} Lee 2000, Ex. A.4(k)
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              First observe that we have an inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(S \cap f^{-1}(T)) \subseteq f(S) \cap T
              \:
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} defining property
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\big(S \cap f^{-1}(T)\big) \subseteq f(S)
              and (ii)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∩
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\big(S \cap f^{-1}(T)\big) \subset T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∩
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cap f^{-1}(T) \subseteq S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq B
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(A) \subseteq f(B)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f\big(
                    S \cap f^{-1}(T)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\subseteq\;
                    f\big(
                    f^{-1}(T)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\subseteq\;
                    T
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first step is the functoriality of images with respect to subset inclusions, and the second step is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(T) \subseteq f^{-1}(T)
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              between direct and inverse image.
            %p Now to see that this inclusion is actually an equality…
          %h2#beckchevalley_condition Beck-Chevalley condition
          %p
            The two ways of consecutively forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimages"} preimages
            along maps that form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+diagram"} pullback diagram
            coincide according to Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BeckChevalleyForPreImages"}
            below – a simple example of what is known as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"}> Beck-Chevalley condition
            ”.
          %p
            First to recall our notation: As above, for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \,\in\, Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(S)
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(S)
                is the set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset S
            %li
              %p
                regarded as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                by declaring that there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                precisely if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset B
                as subsets of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \,\colon\, S \longrightarrow T
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            between sets, we obtain the follows three
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            between their
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! \,\coloneqq\, f(-) \,\colon\, \mathcal{P}(S) \longrightarrow \mathcal{P}(T)
              %p
                forms
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
                under
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
